 HISTORY                                                           320 1451
 -------                                                           320 1451
    This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction        320 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA.  320 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for 20% porous graphite was    320 1451
    synthesized from the 10% and 30% porous molecular dynamics     320 1451
    models [1, 2, 3]. The coherent elastic cross sections were     320 1451
    assumed to be that for a crystalline graphite structure. Ten   320 1451
    temperatures are available in this library. The Full Law       320 1451
    Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to     320 1451
    produce File 7 MT = 2, 4 data for graphite [4]. The coherent   320 1451
    elastic data were prepared using the cubic approximation.      320 1451
    MAT=320 and ZA=420 are used for 20% porous graphite.           320 1451
    Elemental AWR and free-atom cross sections are consistent      320 1451
    with 10P/30P reactor graphite libraries, which reflect         320 1451
    ENDF/B-VII.1 natural carbon data [5].                          320 1451
